@ framework/player: what the player throws (code/throws.cpp, ledger F0225).
@ Mods register gates and handlers (modbase/throws.h) instead of hooking
@ these addresses themselves, so several can coexist.

@ Player::canThrow. Entry `push {r4, lr}`, position-independent.
Throws_canThrow:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x007AA954
    symbol:     ModBase::throws::canThrow(void*)
    trampoline: ModBase::throws::canThrow_orig(void*)

@ The ordinary throw: canThrow's test inlined, then the Throw state (called
@ from 0x607965CC). Entry `push {r4-r7, r11, lr}`, position-independent.
Throws_startThrow:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x007AAA00
    symbol:     ModBase::throws::startThrow(void*)
    trampoline: ModBase::throws::startThrow_orig(void*)

@ The Throw state's execute (state 0x60CC4D6C, built at 0x607B3C64): throws
@ again in phase 1 with the test inlined. Entry `push {r4-r6, lr}`, then
@ `vpush {d8}`; the push alone is replayed.
Throws_throwExecute:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x007AAF80
    symbol:     ModBase::throws::throwExecute(void*)
    trampoline: ModBase::throws::throwExecute_orig(void*)

@ Player::createFireBall (corpus: SE_PLY_THROW_ICEBALL_ref). Entry
@ `push {r4, r5, r6, lr}`, position-independent (sdk/data/hookable.csv).
Throws_createFireBall:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x007AABA0
    symbol:     ModBase::throws::createFireBall(void*, int)
    trampoline: ModBase::throws::createFireBall_orig(void*, int)
